.TH KTX_COMPARE 1 "2026-10-27" "ktx (Rust port)" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ktx_compare \- compare two KTX files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ktx
compare [OPTION...] <input\-file1> <input\-file2>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compares the headers, level indices, data format descriptors, metadata, supercompression data
and image content of two KTX files and prints the differences.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-format <format>
text, json or mini\-json.
.TP
.B \-\-content <mode>
raw, image or ignore.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore\-*
Skip parts of the comparison (e.g. \-\-ignore\-metadata).
.TP
.B \-\-per\-pixel\-output all|<n>|none
Report differing pixels or texel blocks with \-\-content image.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
ktx compare a.ktx2 b.ktx2
.fi
.SH NOTES
This is an unofficial Rust port of Khronos KTX\-Software (libktx and the ktx CLI); it is not
the Khronos build of the tool. The complete, current option list is printed by
.B ktx compare \-\-help.
.SH SEE ALSO
ktx(1)
